WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.220
So as we're getting ready before storms strike this

00:00:03.220 --> 00:00:05.400
severe weather season there are some things you can

00:00:05.400 --> 00:00:07.160
do around the house to keep you and your

00:00:07.160 --> 00:00:09.760
family safe. One of the big things is to

00:00:09.760 --> 00:00:11.500
pick out your severe weather shelter.

00:00:12.300 --> 00:00:14.860
Picking out your severe weather shelter is important because

00:00:14.860 --> 00:00:16.980
if the storm hits you want everybody in the

00:00:16.980 --> 00:00:18.740
house to know where to go and what to

00:00:18.740 --> 00:00:20.840
do when it matters in a short period of

00:00:20.840 --> 00:00:23.320
time. What we're looking for in a severe weather

00:00:23.320 --> 00:00:26.340
shelter especially for tornadoes is we want to find

00:00:26.340 --> 00:00:28.860
the lowest floor of your home the most internal

00:00:28.860 --> 00:00:30.980
room. What we really want to do is put

00:00:30.980 --> 00:00:33.840
as many walls as possible between us and the

00:00:33.840 --> 00:00:36.580
outside world because those walls are going to absorb

00:00:36.580 --> 00:00:39.260
damage so that damage doesn't hit the people inside.

00:00:39.920 --> 00:00:42.680
Once you have that space picked out it's important

00:00:42.680 --> 00:00:46.000
to communicate that shelter space with your entire family.

00:00:46.480 --> 00:00:48.400
Everybody in the house should know where to go

00:00:48.400 --> 00:00:50.680
and what to do when it matters so that

00:00:50.680 --> 00:00:52.980
we can all stay safe this severe weather season.
